  2	//! efficient way, provided the keys are sequential. Largely inspired by
  3	//! Uniswap's [merkle-distributor].
  4	//!
  5	//! `BitMap` packs 256 booleans across each bit of a single 256-bit slot of
  6	//! `U256` type. Hence, booleans corresponding to 256 _sequential_ indices
  7	//! would only consume a single slot, unlike the regular boolean which would
  8	//! consume an entire slot for a single value.
  9	//!
 10	//! This results in gas savings in two ways:
 11	//!
 12	//! - Setting a zero value to non-zero only once every 256 times
 13	//! - Accessing the same warm slot for every 256 _sequential_ indices
 14	//!
 15	//! [merkle-distributor]: https://github.com/Uniswap/merkle-distributor/blob/master/contracts/MerkleDistributor.sol
 16	use alloc::{vec, vec::Vec};
 17	
