177	/// (301): 0 < s < secp256k1n ÷ 2 + 1, and for v in (302): v ∈ {27, 28}.
178	///
179	/// Most signatures from current libraries generate a unique signature
180	/// with an s-value in the lower half order.
181	///
182	/// If your library generates malleable signatures,
183	/// such as s-values in the upper range, calculate a new s-value
184	/// with 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFEBAAEDCE6AF48A03BBFD25E8CD0364141 -
185	/// s1, and flip v from 27 to 28 or vice versa.
